 "meta": {
  "title": "HAZOP and LOPA of the PVC-CONV unit",
  "group": "",
  "date": "2026-11-22",
  "course": "",
  "company": "",
  "bu": "",
  "facility": "PVC-CONV",
  "pid": "",
  "scope": "From the D-100 outlet and the blower suction (F-101, K-101, E-101, FE-101) through the rotary feeder RV-101, the stepped DN150/DN200 conveying line and the diverters DV-102/DV-103 to the storage silos D-201A/B with their bag filters, vents and outlets, including the cooling water to E-101, instrument air and electrical power. The dryer upstream and the bagging and compounding lines downstream are excluded.",
  "objective": "Identify the hazards and operability problems of the unit, judge their risk, and decide what must be added or changed. For the scenarios that need more than the existing safeguards, check the risk reduction by LOPA.",
  "assump": "The unit is operated by trained staff at design (18 t/h, FT-101 0.98 kg/s, PT-102 47.3 kPa g, v/v_salt 1.24 after the step). Cooling water, instrument air and power are available at start-up. Instruments, trips (I-1, I-2) and PSV-101 are tested on the plan in the maintenance procedure.",
  "procName": "",
  "procNo": "",
  "procRev": "",
  "dateStart": "",
  "dateEnd": "",
  "comments": "",
  "protocol": "Method: HAZOP to IEC 61882 with full recording. The team takes one node at a time, states its design intent, and applies the guide words to each parameter to find deviations. For each deviation it records the causes, the events that follow, the consequences without credit for safeguards, the existing safeguards, and the risk after safeguards (S × L). Rows above the tolerable level go to LOPA in the same worksheet: initiating-event frequency, enabling conditions and conditional modifiers, independent protection layers with their PFD, and the mitigated frequency compared with the tolerable event likelihood for the severity. Open points go to the Parking Lot; actions become recommendations with an owner and a due date.",
  "notes": ""
 },
